r523 (F137). Staging (`cdsmnqxtyyoeoznmbidd`) only. Production was not touched. SQL is staged in this PR and has not been applied. Do not squash-merge until Craig approves go-live.

Extends the helper that is already live on staging, `note_fee_sublet_521` (pit fee / weigh / fuel-tank, check F135, sort 305, pin count 234). The r522 script in git creates `note_fee_sublet_522` and expects the pre-fee function bodies. Do not run that r522 script on this staging database. This release calls the Perth helper beside the live 521 helper. Open PR #498 (named external sublets, stale r516 / F130) is not merged. PR #501 is not merged. PR #506 is r524 / F138 and does not use r523 / F137. Department 135 and `app.js` are unchanged.

## What Craig asked

A job-card / import line containing PERTH DELIVERY is external Sublet. It is not a new station and not Needs Review / `JOB_CARD_NOTES`.

Stocks 13042994 and 13092999 are the known cards. On staging today each PERTH DELIVERY line is `JOB_CARD_NOTES`, information only, so the review treats it as Needs Review and Approve stops (the allow-list is the eight workshop stations, and a notes line has no hours). SUBLET is already allowed and does not require hours.

## Rule

`pdc_work_categories_private.perth_delivery_sublet_523` matches the whole operation line (description plus operation code, whitespace collapsed, uppercased). It does not read a GP PO item on another line.

Matches: PERTH DELIVERY, Perth Delivery, extra spaces, TO PERTH DELIVERY, Pre-Delivery (Commercial) PERTH DELIVERY, and operation code PERTH DELIVERY.

Stays on its own rule: KARRATHA DELIVERY, PRE-DELIVERY, Pre-Delivery (Commercial) alone, pit fee, PITS - REFER BRYCE, DELIVERY TO PERTH.

The line is Sublet on the New Vehicles review and on the approve payload. `information_only` is false. A line override, a booking, an owner review or a manual lock still wins. `approve_pdc_new_vehicle_review` and `approve_pdc_new_vehicle_review_446` are not replaced.

